/state.json","size_bytes":213}},"finished_at":"2026-11-23T09:30:09.848901+00:00","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-pq.1","local_name":"bob-cli-pq.1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-pq","agent_clan_generation":"20261123035525","bead_id":"bob-cli-pq.1","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-pq[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Task requirements wear the criterion diamond[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every task requirement is drawn with one quiet, constant-width [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]diamond in its owner's ink, at every depth, in Obsidian, Bob Mac [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Capture, the successor cards, and CLI text. The mark's fill shows [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]the requirement's state, indentation alone shows its depth, and the[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Mac draft shows honest bytes. Nothing about how requirements [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]behave, are stored, or are typed changes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]task_reqs_criterion_diamond.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/task_reqs_criterion_diamond.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-pq[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-pq/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The requirement mark becomes a token in bob-cli and the plugin[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]twins[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]glyph-contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]glyph-contract: req_run becomes a per-state text glyph, the CLI strings [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and RV vectors carry the diamond, the close-card glyph becomes the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`requirement` token, the contract page gets the full rendering spec, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the plugin twins and vector copies change in lockstep so every gate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stays green.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bob annotates requirement lines in previews and the idle [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]agenda[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]line-annotations[dim] · [dim][/dim]after glyph-contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]line-annotations: an additive `req: {depth, state}` object on capture [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]preview block lines and idle-agenda lines, computed by the recognizer, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]so the Mac can draw the diamond without inferring anything from `[ ]`.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Obsidian draws the criterion diamond in notes[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]obsidian-marks[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]obsidian-marks: bob-ledger-tools replaces the hash-run mask with four [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]diamond masks in a constant 1em slot, state by fill, owner ink, the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]verified display fixes, real tooltips, a click guard that teaches [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instead of ticking, the shared card mark, and a light/dark taste pass.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Obsidian successor cards wear the diamond[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]obsidian-cards[dim] · [dim][/dim]after glyph-contract, obsidian-marks[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]obsidian-cards: Navigation Hotkeys draws the shared mark on requirement [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows and the group heading, flips it with the staged verdict, and uses a[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]diamond header icon on requirements-only cards.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The Mac draft shows requirement bytes as a teal chip[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-editor[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-editor: Bob Mac Capture deletes the hash overlay, the byte [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]concealment, and its caret-reveal plumbing, and paints the real `[ ]` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bytes as a teal chip like the existing route and theme washes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Mac previews, agenda, and Pull-In card draw the diamond[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-diamonds[dim] · [dim][/dim]after glyph-contract, line-annotations, mac-editor[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-diamonds: one SwiftUI requirement mark drawn from bob's state in the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]live preview, the idle agenda, and the Pull-In card rows, header, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]filter, with staged-verdict flips, regenerated fixtures, and updated Mac[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Memory records for the criterion diamond[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]memory[dim] · [dim][/dim]after obsidian-cards, mac-diamonds[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory: apply only the accepted memory decisions with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]/sase_memory_write, then regenerate memory and the glossary page.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-pq","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-pq.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_